 <td class="lbl">Product(s)</td><td class="val">{% comment %}
 A tick list, not a text box and not a single select: a case covers several products
 (AD-190). Checkboxes rather than <select multiple> for the reason the Code App's panel uses
 them - a multi-select shows a few rows, needs ctrl-click for a second, and drops the rest
 of the selection on a mis-click.

 The container carries data-ot-hdr-SET rather than data-ot-hdr: it is not one input with a
 value, so the collector reads its boxes instead. The whole set is sent, because a payload
 of additions could never remove one.
{% endcomment %}<div class="ot-hdr-set" data-ot-hdr-set="al_productids" role="group" aria-label="Products">{% for o in products.results.entities %}{% assign okey = '|' | append: o.al_listoptionid | append: '|' %}<label class="ot-hdr-set__item"><input type="checkbox" value="{{ o.al_listoptionid }}" {% if held_product_ids contains okey %}checked{% endif %} /> {{ o.al_name | escape }}</label>{% endfor %}{% comment %}
 A product the case already carries that is no longer offered stays ticked, so saving any
 other header field does not quietly drop it - the server leaves an already-attached option
 alone for the same reason. Marked "(retired)" only when the offered list actually loaded:
 if it came back empty, all that is known is that the catalogue is unavailable.
{% endcomment %}{% for h in case_products.results.entities %}{% assign hkey = '|' | append: h.al_listoptionid | append: '|' %}{% unless offered_product_ids contains hkey %}<label class="ot-hdr-set__item"><input type="checkbox" value="{{ h.al_listoptionid }}" checked /> {{ h.al_name | escape }}{% if products_any %} (retired){% endif %}</label>{% endunless %}{% endfor %}</div></td>
