 {% comment %}
 The checklist, re-read live, so an edit made minutes ago is on the form now
 (project owner, 2026-09-21: "the changes should show immediately after they are
 made").

 Why this is needed at all. Power Pages renders from a server-side cache and learns
 about a Dataverse write through change tracking, which is polled and eventually
 consistent - AD-094 measured the refresh at up to fifteen minutes and AD-117
 concluded that "a longer delay narrows the window and cannot close it". Change
 tracking is enabled on al_question, al_questionversion and al_section and was
 re-verified on 2026-09-21; it makes the portal ABLE to notice, not prompt about it.
 So a question retyped in the Code App - AD-123 checklist administration - can leave
 this page drawing the previous scale for a quarter of an hour.

 That is not only untidy. ResponseGuardPlugin refuses an answer written against a
 superseded version ("This question has been replaced by a newer version"), so a
 checker working from a stale form ticks a box and is told no, with nothing on the
 page to explain why. Their answer is never silently lost - the refusal is the
 server doing its job - but the page has to stop putting them in that position.

 The fix is the one this site already uses for the stale case-status badge on OT
 Remediation: ask the Web API. The Web API is not the Liquid render cache, which is
 the whole point of reading through it here. Webapi/al_questionversion/enabled was
 turned on for this; it grants nothing new, because the Question Version - read
 table permission is read-only and the Web API cannot exceed it.

 ONLY on an unsubmitted review. A submitted one is read as of its submission day
 (BR-013) and must keep rendering the versions it was answered against - refreshing
 it would relabel answered history, which is the opposite of what the versioning is
 for.

 Progressive enhancement throughout: a failure, a refusal, or a browser that never
 runs this leaves the server-rendered form exactly as it was. A stale form is what
 we already have, so there is nothing to lose by failing quietly, and nothing here
 is a permission decision the page is entitled to make (NFR-SEC-01).
 {% endcomment %}
 <p class="ot-stale" data-ot-checklist-stale hidden role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
 {% comment %}
 The scales, emitted from the same literals the rendering uses, so the script does
 not become a third hand-written copy of them. "inline" matches OT Answer Options,
 which is what draws every answer cell; "grid" matches the tick-column headings
 chosen above. 120910006 reads its third option differently on a Tax review
 (AD-055 amended), so the discipline is resolved here rather than in script.
 portalChecklistFreshness.test.ts pins these against both sources.
 {% endcomment %}
 <script type="application/json" data-ot-scales>
 {
 "inline": {
 "120910005": { "values": [120910300,120910301], "labels": ["PASS","FAIL"] },
 {% if is_tax_review %}
